 justify-center text-white text-lg font-bold shrink-0 shadow-md">9</div><span class="text-white font-medium">Corrective action</span></div></div></div></div></section><section class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-white"><div class="container mx-auto px-6"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto"><div class="text-center mb-12"><h2 class="heading-font text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-2">Benefits and Considerations</h2><p class="text-slate-600">Practical advantages and implementation considerations under PED 2014/68/EU.</p></div><div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8"><div><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-eurogold-600 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2"><i class="fas fa-check-circle"></i> 9.1 Key Advantages of PED 2014/68/EU</h3><div class="space-y-3"><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 bg-eurogold-50/40 rounded-lg border border-eurogold-200"><i class="fas fa-check text-eurogold-600 mt-1"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Free trade of conforming pressure equipment across all EU/EEA member states without requiring separate national approvals</span></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 bg-eurogold-50/40 rounded-lg border border-eurogold-200"><i class="fas fa-check text-eurogold-600 mt-1"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Harmonised safety requirements create a level playing field for manufacturers</span></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 bg-eurogold-50/40 rounded-lg border border-eurogold-200"><i class="fas fa-check text-eurogold-600 mt-1"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Manufacturers can freely choose their conformity assessment module (within their equipment category)</span></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 bg-eurogold-50/40 rounded-lg border border-eurogold-200"><i class="fas fa-check text-eurogold-600 mt-1"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Manufacturers can freely choose from any EU-designated Notified Body</span></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 bg-eurogold-50/40 rounded-lg border border-eurogold-200"><i class="fas fa-check text-eurogold-600 mt-1"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Clear, category-based classification provides proportionate regulatory burden - lower hazard equipment faces lighter requirements</span></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 bg-eurogold-50/40 rounded-lg border border-eurogold-200"><i class="fas fa-check text-eurogold-600 mt-1"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Standardised EU Declaration of Conformity template (provided by PED-ADCO) simplifies documentation</span></div></div></div><div><h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-amber-600 mb-4 flex items-center gap-2"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i> 9.2 Challenges and Practical Considerations</h3><div class="space-y-3"><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 bg-amber-50 rounded-lg border border-amber-200"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle text-amber-600 mt-1"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Varying experience levels and interpretations among different Notified Bodies can create inconsistencies</span></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 bg-amber-50 rounded-lg border border-amber-200"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle text-amber-600 mt-1"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Not all pressure equipment is covered by harmonised EN standards, requiring use of European Material Approvals or other approved methods</span></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 bg-amber-50 rounded-lg border border-amber-200"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle text-amber-600 mt-1"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Different national requirements for in-service inspection and operation may still apply in individual member states beyond the scope of the Directive</span></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 bg-amber-50 rounded-lg border border-amber-200"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle text-amber-600 mt-1"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Manufacturers exporting to Great Britain (GB) must also address UKCA marking requirements, though CE marking is currently accepted in GB indefinitely following UK Government announcements in 2023-2024</span></div><div class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 bg-amber-50 rounded-lg border border-amber-200"><i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle text-amber-600 mt-1"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Qualification of welding procedures and personnel per EN standards can be time-consuming for new manufacturers</span></div></div></div></div></div></div></section><section class="py-20 lg:py-28 bg-gradient-to-br from-euro-50 via-white to-eurogold-50/40 relative overflow-hidden"><div class="absolute inset-0 pointer-events-none"><div class="absolute top-0 right-0 w-96 h-96 bg-eurogold-200/30 rounded-full blur-3xl"></div><div class="absolute bottom-0 left-0 w-80 h-80 bg-euro-200/30 rounded-full blur-3xl"></div></div><div class="container mx-auto px-6 relative z-10"><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto text-center p-10 lg:p-14 bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-50 to-white backdrop-blur-md border border-slate-100 rounded-[2.5rem] shadow-xl"><h4 class="heading-font text-xs text-euro-600 font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.4em] mb-4">Support</h4><h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-4">How Eurotech Can Help</h2><p class="text-slate-600 text-lg mb-6 max-w-3xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">Eurotech Assessment and Certification Services Private Limited provides comprehensive support to manufacturers seeking PED 2014/68/EU certification. Our services include:</p><div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto mb-8"><ul class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-left"><li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 rounded-xl bg-white/90 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm"><i class="fas fa-check-circle text-eurogold-600 mt-0.5"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Gap analysis and readiness assessment against PED 2014/68/EU requirements</span></li><li class="flex items-start gap-3 p-3 rounded-xl bg-white/90 border border-slate-200 shadow-sm"><i class="fas fa-check-circle text-eurogold-600 mt-0.5"></i><span class="text-slate-700">Guidance on correct equipment classification and selection of 